usage: test-diagnostic-export.py [-h] --binary BINARY --evidence EVIDENCE
                                 [--cases {refusals,local,logs,write-failure,sigint,sigterm,publication-race,backpressure} [{refusals,local,logs,write-failure,sigint,sigterm,publication-race,backpressure} ...]]

Actual private diagnostic CLI lifecycle checks; no builds or host USB. Linux
x86_64/aarch64 ordinary-UID subprocesses. A ptrace syscall-entry gate holds
one actual fresh partial-file fchmod or fsync without altering registers,
results or file bytes. It tests removable observer delays, not kernel
hardblock.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --binary BINARY
  --evidence EVIDENCE
  --cases {refusals,local,logs,write-failure,sigint,sigterm,publication-race,backpressure} [{refusals,local,logs,write-failure,sigint,sigterm,publication-race,backpressure} ...]
